[size=5][b]Find The Needle co-op mod[/b][/size]

Adds co-op multiplayer to the demo. Several players dig the same haystack,
share the money and see each other's buildings.

Connections go through Steam's relay network, so there is no port forwarding
and no IP addresses to exchange. The host invites from the Steam friends list.

[size=4][b]What is synced[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The haystack. Everyone digs the same pile.
[*]Buildings, placed and demolished.
[*]Money, debt, hay sold, needles found, the collection.
[*]The tech tree.
[*]Uncovered needles. They show up for everyone and can only be handed in once.
[*]New hay loads, which resync every client.
[*]Player positions, names and the tool in hand.
[/list]
There is in-game chat (Y) and a resync key (F8). The panel does not show IP
addresses, Steam IDs or lobby codes, so it is safe to have on screen while
streaming.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Find The Needle demo (free on Steam), build V26 or newer
[*]Windows 64-bit
[*]The same mod version on every machine
[*]The game has to be launched from Steam, or the invites will not work
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Unzip the download.
[*]Copy the [b]mods[/b] folder next to [b]FindTheNeedle.exe[/b]. In Steam:
right-click the game, Manage, Browse local files.
[*]Open [b]override.cfg[/b], in that same folder, with any text editor and add
these two lines at the end:
[code][autoload]
MPMod="*mods/multiplayer/mp.gd"[/code]
If the file already has an [autoload] section, only the second line is needed.
[*]Launch from Steam. There is a MULTIPLAYER entry in the main menu.
[/list]
There is no installer to run and the download contains no scripts. To
uninstall, delete that line and the mods folder.

Game updates replace override.cfg, so add the lines again after each one.

[size=4][b]Playing[/b][/size]
Host: MULTIPLAYER, CREATE GAME, INVITE FRIENDS, then start or load a save as
usual. Everyone else joins by accepting the Steam invite.

[size=4][b]Known limitations[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Machines that take hay from the pile on their own (piston rake, robotic arm,
drone, scanner) only run on the host. On clients they stand still. Running them
everywhere counted hay and money twice.
[*]Loose props (buckets, sacks, bales) are local to each player.
[*]Machine settings such as filters and switches are not synced.
[*]Bought tools are per player. Money is shared.
[*]Only the host saves. Clients never write to their own save files.
[*]The online leaderboard is disabled while the mod is loaded.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Source[/b][/size]
